conformance
  headwater/standard 3.2.0
  no digest pinned
  at 2026-08-12

rules
  pin.current gap
    The pin names the package that is installed
    the version is 3.2.0 and there is no digest on either side. The package
    directory carries no release record, so no published artifact stands behind
    it
    fix: Five steps reach this rule, and a consumer cannot take the first one
         from inside this tool. Step 1 is a published artifact. `headwater
         taxonomy publish --out <dir>` writes one and prints its digest. A
         consumer needs the artifact that the publisher of the package wrote,
         and no verb of this engine fetches one. The publisher records that gap
         as HW-OBL-0085. Step 2 writes the printed digest into `taxonomy.digest`
         in `.headwater/taxonomy.yml`. Step 3 moves the existing
         `.headwater/packages/<name>` directory aside. Step 4 runs `headwater
         taxonomy vendor <dir>`, which checks the artifact against the pin and
         installs it under `.headwater/packages/`. That install goes to the same
         path step 3 cleared, and it refuses to overwrite a directory that
         carries no release record. Step 5 runs `headwater taxonomy resolve`,
         because a vendored artifact replaces the taxonomy sources and moves the
         lock. A publisher that consumes the package it maintains does not have
         to lose the source to close this gap, but it does have to move it: keep
         the authored files outside `.headwater/packages/<name>` and publish
         from there with `--from <dir>` on step 1, because
         `.headwater/packages/<name>` is where step 4 writes and a directory
         both authored and vendored is the one case `taxonomy vendor` cannot
         tell apart from a package somebody still maintains. Where the source
         stays inside `.headwater/packages/<name>`, a dated waiver is the honest
         answer instead.
  lock.current met
    The lock is current against the taxonomy sources
  gates.required not decided
    A gate runs this engine between a change and a merge
    no reading of a tree decides this, and no attestation record exists yet. It
    is neither met nor missing
    fix: Record an attestation and name the gate it ran in.
  corpus.classified gap
    Every document of the corpus is classified
    4 of 201 rows carry no kind
    fix: Declare a kind that claims the rows, or move them off the shelf the
         corpus root names.
  projections.current gap
    Every projection is current against the corpus
    the obligation register is stale against 2 records
    fix: Run `headwater generate`.

levels
  L0 Vendored and the lock is current against it — not reached, 0 of 1 rules met
